<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samborides</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Samborides were a dynasty that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerelia">Pomerelia</a>, the region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gdansk">Gdańsk</a> on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a>, from the 12th century until 1294. At first governors for the Polish dukes, they became independent under Świętopełk II, who took the ducal title in 1227. The line ended with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mestwin-ii">Mestwin II</a>, who left his lands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/przemysl-ii">Przemysł II</a> of Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samborides.jpg" alt="Samborides" width="320" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Artemis Andromeda · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Empty_fleur-de-lis_French_shield.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
